notes:
The two-room split. 92x128 -> 80x84, area2 16,384 -> 7,056 (x0.43), ticks 267,010 -> 262,399.
Room A = init + phase 2; room B = phase 3 + emit + no-solution. The seam is real: phase 3 and
emit need only ring V and the O pipe, never ring B, so room B's interior is 33 against room A's
41. Ring B lives in the void BELOW room A (room A is 60 rows against room B's 74, so it is free)
rather than in a widened band above. The relay room disappears entirely: a pipe may not loop back
into its own room, which was the only reason ring V needed a turnaround — A -> B -> A is legal.

THE UNMEASURED NUMBER CAME BACK FREE. The design budgeted +5% for the idle-relay forwarding cost.
Measured by swapping ring V's relay on the real grid: relay(3,3)=8.00 ticks/word, (4,3)=5.00,
(6,4)=3.20, (8,6)=2.67 — all four gave an IDENTICAL 267,010-tick average. Ring V's far side is
never on the critical path: 28 words against a ~1,500-tick lap in a 97-cell pipe, so the buffer
absorbs the bursts. Ticks then improved 4,600 because _nosol stops being a 97-row walk to the
bottom of the grid.

Two silent failures the guards caught, both of which loaded and ran:
  - Room A's forwarding loop used the one-room v band (14..24), but room A's baton anchor is at
    column 9 and ring V's send anchor at 21, so the midpoint is 15: every ring-V word room A
    forwarded after handover went down the BATON pipe. Right shape, wrong values. _op now does an
    exact nearest-anchor check requiring a strict win (ties go to reading order, which nothing may
    depend on) and it is a build error, pinned by a test.
  - _rot's third exit: its X goes straight on a word of exactly zero, which never happens in the
    one-room build because the ring is always aligned — but room B starts wherever the idle loop
    left it, and both RR before phase 2 and C when the last mask wins are zero. Straight walked
    into the wall.
  - _mouths counted eight when ring B's serpentine put a bend under the relay's corner.

The baton is a third pipe polled with q, not a sentinel in ring V: a marker costs ~10 ticks/word
against 6 because every word then needs M 2 + X W to be compared without being destroyed, which
doubles ring V's cost on every lap of the search.

Remaining: room B alone sets the charged side (74 rows against room A's 60; 84 tall against 80
wide). Four rows off room B is area2 7,056 -> 6,400, ~x0.91, and all four must come out of the
phase-3-and-emit stack, already greedily compacted once.

